---
import Ide from "./_Ide.astro";
import Page from "./_Page.astro";
import { PY_SNIPPET, TERM_SNIPPET } from "./_samples";

export const prerender = false;
---

<Page
  title="Client runner"
  lead="Mini-IDE for notes, exam answers and grading. Static mock: the editor stands in for CodeMirror 6 (VS Code Dark+ theme) and the terminal for xterm.js. Nothing here runs."
>
  <section class="mt-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">The component</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
      One box: toolbar, editor, terminal, status row. The terminal stays attached below the editor in every mode so the
      output is always next to the code that produced it.
    </p>
    <Ide mode="snippet" language="python" code={PY_SNIPPET} state="done" terminal={TERM_SNIPPET} lastRun="0.4 s" />
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Pages</h2>
    <ul class="menu mt-2 rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100">
      <li><a href="/design/playground/client-runner/modes">Modes: snippet, answer (Python, Prolog), review</a></li>
      <li><a href="/design/playground/client-runner/states">States: download, running, input, errors, limits, autosave</a></li>
      <li><a href="/design/playground/client-runner/exam">Exam density: six questions, five editors</a></li>
      <li><a href="/design/playground/client-runner/mobile">Mobile: stacked and tabbed layouts</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Visual decisions</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm">
      <li>Editor and terminal keep a fixed dark palette regardless of the app theme, as code editors usually do.</li>
      <li>Run is a soft success button, Stop a soft error button, in the same slot. Submit keeps the only primary button.</li>
      <li>The terminal header carries the process state (running, waiting for input, exit code) so the toolbar stays small.</li>
      <li>The status row only appears in answer mode, and only when there is something to say (save time, sync warning).</li>
      <li>Blocking states (download failed, execution disabled, draft conflict) take the terminal's or editor's place, not a modal.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Page>
